**(a) Legislation (2 marks).** Laws on ICT (for example data protection, computer misuse, copyright and electronic-communications laws; in Cameroon the 2010 law on cybersecurity and cybercriminality) are useful because they:

- protect the privacy of individuals and the personal data held about them, and give people the right to see and correct their data;
- make hacking, virus spreading, software piracy, online fraud and identity theft criminal offences, which can be punished, and so discourage them;
- protect the intellectual property of software authors and give legal value to electronic transactions and signatures, which builds trust in e-commerce and e-government.

**(b) Ergonomics (2 marks).** Ergonomics is the study of how to design equipment and the working environment so that they fit the people who use them. In ICT it is useful because it prevents health problems (back and neck pain, eye strain, headaches, repetitive strain injury of the hands and wrists) and so increases comfort, safety and productivity of the users. It is applied through adjustable chairs, screens at eye level with anti-glare filters, ergonomic keyboards and wrist rests, good lighting and ventilation, enough space, and regular breaks.
